"text_chars": 943, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "2f93089f-a400-4099-9eb8-68fac0a7f724", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790233713.1864681, "updated_at": 1790233720.793291, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yeah, so on the 21st it took the 11 bucks. On the 23rd it took the 6 bucks. Two separate transactions, $17 total.", "text_chars": 113, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "c305757c-230d-4b3d-928f-ed720ed7a182", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790233714.586117, "updated_at": 1790233720.130427, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yep. Then we can reconcile it cleanly:\n\n**Albert has already debited $17 total from the bank:**\n- **9/21:** $11\n- **9/23:** $6\n- **Total outstanding/in transit: $17**\n\nThe screenshot is specifically showing the **$11 transfer initiated 9/17** as still “Processing,” despite the bank debit occurring 9/21. The **$6 is a second transfer**, so we should assume that one may also remain in Albert's settlement pipeline.\n\nSo **$17 is the number we're tracking**, not $11. I wouldn't treat either amount as available cash until it actually settles into Albert, and I wouldn't consider Albert ready for cancellation until both transfers resolve. Once they do: **recover the $17 → disable Auto Save → cancel the paid membership/account → verify no further debits.**\n\nThat also explains why this thing has been such a pain: they're continuing to pull Auto Save transactions while the earlier one hasn't even finished displaying as settled. memcite", "text_chars": 940, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "3e6ecdb8-e4f6-4add-89ba-ad3a2a28f1ba", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790233758.304034, "updated_at": 1790233778.552114, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yeah, I turned that auto-save off. We need to get those transactions out. I can't cancel it. I gotta try to file a dispute for the 19.99 that they charged me when I wanted to cancel.", "text_chars": 182, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "b80ea877-9879-48ee-800a-ed250b1e45e3", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790233761.200203, "updated_at": 1790233778.47005, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Exactly. **Auto Save is off**, so we've stopped the leak. Now there are two separate issues:\n\n- **$17 savings transfers:** $11 debited 9/21 + $6 debited 9/23. Those need to finish settling into Albert so you can withdraw/recover the money.\n- **$19.99 charge:** separate issue. If that was a membership/subscription charge assessed while you were trying to cancel, preserve the cancellation attempts/screenshots and dispute the charge through Albert first; if they don't resolve it, you can pursue the dispute through the funding bank/card issuer as appropriate.\n\nI would **not dispute the $11 or $6 as unauthorized right now** if you recognize them as Auto Save transfers—the money should still belong to you and be recoverable once Albert finishes processing. The **$19.99 is the charge to challenge**.\n\nAnd we should keep the cancellation sequence tight: **$17 settles → withdraw $17 → confirm $0 balance/no pending transfers → cancel Albert → verify no further debits → pursue/finish the $19.99 dispute.** memcite", "text_chars": 1018, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "d8d303c2-afb8-44ba-bc2b-f7f9eab38f62", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790295425.999696, "updated_at": 1790295431.409916, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["image_asset_pointer", "text"], "text": " So this should get back to our account tomorrow.", "text_chars": 49, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["image_asset_pointer"]}, {"message_id": "708d89f0-d107-4c01-b9b9-c6546d1ebb7e", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790295428.30248, "updated_at": 1790295428.30248, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "model_editable_context", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "8b7b7c17-704a-4737-8fe1-dce449aefa99", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790295428.326563, "updated_at": 1790295431.28891, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yes — **tomorrow, Friday 9/25, is the date I’d expect the $11 to finally clear**, based on Albert’s own stated **5–6 business-day** window.\n\nOne distinction: this screenshot shows the money moving **from your bank into Albert**, not back to your bank. So once it flips from **Processing → Completed**, we still need to **withdraw it from Albert back to your bank**.\n\nAnd we have **$17 total** to recover: the **$11 + $6**. Once both settle, pull the full $17 out. Then we can finish killing the Albert account and deal separately with that **$19.99 charge**. memcite", "text_chars": 568, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "517f40b6-d8df-486b-9769-a3e6829b91a6", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790295452.474055, "updated_at": 1790295458.210802, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "I can remove the 11, right? So the thing is, is I need the 11 for the hotel tomorrow.", "text_chars": 85, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "233def7c-d5f5-4ddd-9f6b-e4d24a13ab49", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790295454.382932, "updated_at": 1790295454.382932, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "model_editable_context", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "ba5530ce-9796-453b-bcdd-0060e1f23d63", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790295454.385969, "updated_at": 1790295457.775423, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yes — **once that $11 changes from “In Progress” to “Completed” and appears in your available Albert savings balance, you should be able to initiate a withdrawal back to your linked bank.**\n\nBut there’s an important timing issue for the hotel tomorrow: **“Completed” into Albert does not necessarily mean the $11 will be back in your bank tomorrow.** A normal withdrawal from Albert could itself take additional processing time.\n\nSo for tomorrow’s hotel money, I **wouldn’t count the $11 as usable yet**. If Albert offers an **instant-transfer option** once it clears, that could change things. Otherwise, we should keep tomorrow’s hotel cash plan assuming this $11 is unavailable, and treat it as upside if we can get it out quickly.", "text_chars": 734, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "b557b3f2-2df9-4003-a43b-b3c4ece9121b", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790295471.075686, "updated_at": 1790295477.103331, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Well no, can't they do it instant? It's hooked up to my SoFi card. Doesn't Albert do instant?", "text_chars": 93, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "2c77006b-a5b3-4072-895f-5eb0aaaec1e0", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790295472.779122, "updated_at": 1790295472.779122, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "web", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 1, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "69beaa9a-df07-4047-9fae-1988f1e20fe6", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at