935168, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "**Yes, Albert does have instant transfers in some circumstances.** The key question is whether it offers **Instant** as a withdrawal option for *this particular $11* once the incoming Auto Save transfer is fully settled.\n\nBecause your **SoFi debit card is linked**, there’s a reasonable chance Albert will offer the debit-card/instant route. But I don't want to tell you the $11 is definitely available instantly until Albert actually marks it **Completed**—their help documentation wasn't surfaced clearly enough for me to verify that every Savings withdrawal qualifies.\n\nSo tomorrow, the moment that $11 flips to **Completed**, go into the withdrawal/transfer screen. **If it gives you an “Instant” option to the SoFi debit card, use that**, and that could make the $11 usable for the hotel tomorrow rather than waiting another ACH cycle.\n\nSend me the screen when it clears and **we'll know immediately whether the instant route is available.**", "text_chars": 946, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "ddfcee5f-3549-4b86-8087-512afdfb6dcd", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790295516.637244, "updated_at": 1790295521.974982, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["image_asset_pointer", "text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 1, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["image_asset_pointer"]}, {"message_id": "6915ee81-a464-40ab-8de9-cf90df5e29cf", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790295518.810644, "updated_at": 1790295521.792933, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "**There it is.** This screen changes things.\n\nAlbert is already showing **Albert Savings: $17.00** — exactly the **$11 + $6** we've been tracking. So the full $17 is recognized in the savings balance even though that individual $11 transaction screen still says “In Progress.”\n\nThe next move is to tap **Albert Savings → Transfer/Withdraw** and see what withdrawal methods it offers. If it gives you **Instant to your linked SoFi/debit card**, then yes—we should be able to pull the money without waiting for another multi-day ACH cycle.\n\n**Don't cancel Albert yet.** Get that $17 out first. If you send me the next transfer screen, I'll walk it with you.", "text_chars": 655, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "e265a699-605e-4869-9fc6-c8675215474e", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790295539.6875591, "updated_at": 1790295553.855177, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "I can't withdraw yet. That's what I showed you the other screen. No, what I'm trying to say is once it hits 11, I can put it in Albert cash and instantly transfer, I think, to my SoFi.", "text_chars": 184, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "10274237-a2df-48c0-92b8-b56b3c01825d", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790295541.278576, "updated_at": 1790295550.540605, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Ah — **yes. I understand what you're saying now.** You're not trying to withdraw